 Implemented protected Transaction History at:

  GET /wallets/:id/transactions

  Supports:

  - Owner-only access via JWT
  - Pagination: page, limit
  - Filters: type=deposit|withdraw|transfer, fromDate, toDate
  - Sorting: sortBy=createdAt|amount, sortOrder=asc|desc
  - TypeORM query builder with stable secondary ordering
  - Required { data, meta } response contract
  - Invalid wallet ID/date/range, missing wallet, and unauthorized owner handling
  - Swagger docs at /api/docs

  Key files:

  - History DTO (src/transaction/dto/get-transactions.dto.ts)
  - Response Swagger DTO (src/transaction/dto/transaction-history-response.dto.ts)
  - Controller endpoint (src/wallet/wallet.controller.ts)
  - Query and ownership logic (src/wallet/wallet.service.ts)
  - Swagger/global validation setup (src/main.ts)

  Example:

  GET /wallets/4/transactions?page=1&limit=20&type=transfer&fromDate=2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z&sortBy=amount&sortOrder=desc
  Authorization: Bearer <access-token>

  I also fixed authentication wiring necessary for this protected endpoint, corrected the login handler, and fixed the deposit DTO type that previously broke compilation.

  Verified:

  - npm run build passes
  - npm test -- --runInBand passes: 4 tests covering filtering/pagination, nonexistent wallet, ownership, and invalid date ranges
  - Prettier passes for all changed files

  Full database/Redis e2e execution still needs a configured PostgreSQL and Redis instance.